  "full_response": "Certainly! Please note, storing sensitive information like API tokens, database passwords, and JWT secrets directly in your Kubernetes deployment YAML is not recommended for production environments. These values should be stored securely using Kubernetes secrets.\n\nBelow is an example of a Kubernetes deployment YAML including environment variables for these sensitive values. This example also demonstrates how to reference the secrets from Kubernetes in the deployment.\n\nCreate a Kubernetes Secret for each sensitive piece of information:\n\n1.api-token-secret.yaml`\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: api-token-secret\ntype: Opaque\ndata:\n  API_TOKEN: YWdlIG1wcmVhZ2U=  # Base64 encoded \"exampleAPIToken\"\n  JWT_SIGNING_SECRET: cmVkaXIgYWRkaW5NdmVyc2lvbjE=  # Base64 encoded \"exampleJWTSecret\"\n  DB_PASSWORD: VHJhY3Rpb24=  # Base64 encoded \"exampleDBPassword\"\n```\n\n2. `database-password-secret.yaml`\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: database-password-secret\ntype: Opaque\ndata:\n  DB_PASSWORD: VHJhY3Rpb24=  # Base64 encoded \"exampleDBPassword\"\n```\n\n3. `jwt-signing-secret-secret.yaml`\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: jwt-signing-secret-secret\ntype: Opaque\ndata:\n  JWT_SIGNING_SECRET: cmVkaXIgYWRka5NdmVyc2lvbjE=  # Base64 encoded \"exampleJWTSecret\"\n```\n\nDeploy these secrets:\n\n```sh\nkubectl apply -f api-token-secret.yaml\nkubectl apply -f database-password-secret.yaml\nkubectl apply -f jwt-signing-secret-secret.yaml\n```\n\nNow, here's a sample Kubernetes deployment YAML that references these secrets as environment variables:\n\n4. `deployment.yaml`\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: api-application\n  labels:\n    app: api-application\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: api-application\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: api-application\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: api-application\n        image: yourimage/image\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: ",
